Seagull CES (Crew Evaluation System) tests and answers for marine specialists.
This app for preparing sailors for exams and certification Seagull.
The CES app for your smartphone will help you get familiar with the format of tasks in advance – this simulator will allow you to soberly assess your capabilities and correctly plan your preparation for the exam, focusing on the gaps in knowledge.

 - CES Test is designed to identify background knowledge defined in STCW for all seamen.


 The CES system covers all sections of the STCW, being an indispensable tool for evaluating the knowledge of the crew. One of the main features is extended randomization, which means that questions are not repeated. CES Test is used by more than 350 companies worldwide. 

 The desired level of knowledge of the language is not lower than Pre-Intermediate, with the Intermediate level and higher, the test will be much easier to pass. In addition to a good level of English, competence in the profession is mandatory.


 The questions that make up the CES test are directly related to your specialty and the type of ship you will be working on.

- Oil Tanker. Operational (Deck); 
- Oil Tanker. Support (Deck);
- Oil Tanker. Management (Deck);

- Chemical Tanker. Management (Deck); 
- Chemical Tanker. Operational (Deck);
- Chemical Tanker Support Deck;

- Container. Management (Deck);  
- Container Operational Deck;
- Container Support Deck;

- Anchor Handling. Management (Deck);
- Anchor Handling Operational Deck;
- Anchor Handling Support Deck;

- Anchor Handling (Incl. DP) Management Deck;
- Anchor Handling (Incl. DP) Operational Deck;
- Anchor Handling. Support (Deck);

- Cargo Handling And Stowage

 There are several types of test:

– STCW test
– Detailed Test
– Company Specific (the test determined directly by the shipping company is a unique set of tasks)
– Cargo Handling and Stowage
– Catering
– Controlling operation of ship and care for persons onboard
– Electrical, electronic and control engineering
– Flag State Test
– Maintenance and Repair
– Marine Engineering
– Maritime English (assessment of profiled English language skills)
– Navigation
– Radio Communication GMDSS


Application features:
• Mode "Preparation"
• Mode "Exam"
• Mode "Marathon"
• Questions search

     Advantages:
• The application does not require an Internet connection;
• Tests are always "Available".
• Many modes of work with tests.

This test simulator will help you prepare for the Seagull Crew Evaluation System (CES) - All Tests.

All questions and answers are for educational purposes only.
The app is free with in-app purchases!

For free:
In this application you will be able to pass 10 test questions an unlimited number of times.
Paid:
Full access to all functions will be available after payment!
